meta {
  name: update-staff
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

patch {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/admin/v1/staff/{{new_staff_uid}}
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "role": "manager"
  }
}

tests {
  test("responds 200, or explains the refusal", function () {
    expect([200, 403, 404]).to.include(res.status)
  })
}

docs {
  # Update a staff member

Owner only. Role and status are the two patchable fields.

**Try it against `{{staff_uid}}`** -- your own account, the only owner -- with
`{"role": "staff"}`. It is refused: demoting the last active owner would leave nobody able to manage
staff, which is unrecoverable without direct database access. The same guard applies to
`{"status": "inactive"}`.
}
